{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/844767-social-and-mental-combat-in-2e","id":844767,"title":"Social and Mental Combat in 2e","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-09T15:36:49-08:00","id":844767,"title":"Social and Mental Combat in 2e","content":"I find the rules for social and mental combat from <i>Danse Macabre</i> very interesting. If I wanted to use them in a second edition setting, what about them would need to be updated, do you think? I haven't yet read the second edition Chronicles of Darkness rulebook; is there anything there that would make these redundant? Should social combat completely supplant the rules for social maneuvering? On the one hand, keeping them both in means a bunch of differing subsystems, but on the other, I feel like they model two different things: one is for getting someone to do what you want, while the other is primarily for hurting someone's social standing (and their feelings).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-09T16:16:07-08:00","id":844784,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think Social Chases do what Social Combat wanted to do better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T04:14:04-08:00","id":845006,"title":"","content":"In Chases, you have a basic target number of 5 successes, modified by things like your physical speed, initiative, and size. For social chases, I've basically used the process for &quot;more doors&quot; found in Social Maneuvering to replace the more physical attributes. <br /> <br /> What have the rest of you done for Social Chases? Something similar? Just used base 5?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T09:54:42-07:00","id":846615,"title":"","content":"What are social chase's? I feel like I missed something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2191-kevorkiandoctor","name":"Kevorkiandoctor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T10:34:56-07:00","id":846628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kevorkiandoctor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/844767-social-and-mental-combat-in-2e?p=846615#post846615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are social chase's? I feel like I missed something</div> </div> </div> </div>You can use the Chase rules from the Chronicles of Darkness core rulebook with social actions. As MCN pointed out, you do have to fiddle with the rules a tiny bit, since by default the target number of successes to pursue or evade is base 5 modified by things like the characters' Speed, Size, Initiative, and knowledge of the territory. In a social chase, you'd have to change the modifiers to be based on traits more relevant to socializing. But I think with some minor hacking it could make for a better competitive social subsystem than Social Combat, if you need one.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T21:23:29-07:00","id":847525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MNC</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">What have the rest of you done for Social Chases? Something similar? Just used base 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a big fan of the various social combat rules in theory but have found them cumbersome to use in practice. So I just have characters roll extended, contested Social Attribute + Social Skill checks, requiring successes equal to double each others' Willpower. The winner, PC or NPC, picks a (reasonable) course of action they want the loser to undertake. If the loser gives in and follows it, they take a Beat. If they don't, they lose a point of Willpower and take a roll-penalizing Condition of some kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}